defmodule <%= @web_namespace %>.TurboStream do
  @moduledoc """
  Sends Turbo Streams to the `<turbo-stream-channel-source>` elements rendered
  in a page.

  Each element joins its topic through `TurboStreamChannel` and renders every
  stream it receives. This module owns the wire contract between the server and
  those elements — the `"message"` event carrying the markup under `:data` — so
  nothing else in the app has to know it.

  Build the markup with `TurboComponents.turbo_stream_tag/2` or a
  `turbo_stream` template, then send it with `broadcast/2`.
  """

  @doc """
  Broadcasts already-built `<turbo-stream>` markup to every subscriber of `topic`.

  `topic` is the topic given to `.turbo_stream_channel_source/1`, which signs
  it for `TurboStreamChannel` to verify on join:

      <%= @web_namespace %>.TurboStream.broadcast("turbo_stream:" <> user.id, stream)

  The message goes to every node in the PubSub cluster: a subscriber holds its
  socket on one node, which is rarely the node handling the request that caused
  the change.
  """
  def broadcast(topic, stream) when is_binary(topic) and is_binary(stream) do
    <%= @web_namespace %>.Endpoint.broadcast(topic, "message", %{data: stream})
  end
end
